# evidence-cmd: cd plugins/foundry/mcp-server && uv run --with pytest python -c 'import sys; sys.path[:0]=["src","."]; from tests.orchestration.test_guidance_imperatives import turn_boundary_report; [print(r) for r in turn_boundary_report()]' 2>/dev/null
# evidence-for: ST-001, ST-002, ST-003, CT-002, OT-004

the server-side half of the turn boundary, per run state.
ends-turn: the imperative answers 'YOUR NEXT CALL: NONE'.
names-wake: it names the completion notification as what resumes the lead.
names-call: it names at least one literal tool call.
denies-poll: it forbids a sleep, a poll and a re-call loop by name.

  ST-001 / ST-002  build_castings  live          ends-turn=yes names-wake=yes names-call=yes denies-poll=yes
  ST-001 / ST-002  fix_defects     live          ends-turn=yes names-wake=yes names-call=yes denies-poll=yes
  ST-003           build_castings  idle          ends-turn=no  names-wake=no  names-call=yes denies-poll=n/a
  ST-003           fix_defects     idle          ends-turn=no  names-wake=no  names-call=yes denies-poll=n/a
  ST-003           build_castings  undispatched  ends-turn=no  names-wake=no  names-call=yes denies-poll=n/a
  ST-003           fix_defects     undispatched  ends-turn=no  names-wake=no  names-call=yes denies-poll=n/a

ST-003 is discharged by 'names-call=yes in every state where no agent is
running': a lead that is handed a call cannot park for want of a move.
ST-001 and ST-002 are discharged by 'ends-turn=yes AND names-wake=yes'
on the one state where an agent IS running -- ending the turn is stated
as correct, and the thing that ends the idle is named in the same breath.
The idle of ST-001 and the notification of ST-002 are the HARNESS's to
perform; this casting owns only what the lead is told, and that is all
this log claims.
